@startuml
title MODRISS Operational Change Routing and Lifecycle Re-entry

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

start
:Capture roadmap request, telemetry signal, incident,\nsecurity finding, provider change or cost anomaly;
:Create change-impact record and preserve evidence;

if (Immediate restoration required?) then (yes)
  :Execute incident/recovery procedure;
  :Record temporary downstream change;
else (no)
endif

if (Outcome, requirement or domain meaning changed?) then (yes)
  :Re-enter at CIM;
elseif (Provider-independent architecture changed?) then (yes)
  :Re-enter at PIM;
elseif (AWS realization or deployment changed?) then (yes)
  :Re-enter at PSM;
elseif (Reusable generation logic changed?) then (yes)
  :Re-enter at EGL/EGX generator source;
elseif (Business logic or supported extension changed?) then (yes)
  :Re-enter at artifact/code workflow;
elseif (Promotion, rollback or support control changed?) then (yes)
  :Re-enter at release/operations workflow;
else (method concern)
  :Re-enter at method-engineering backlog;
endif

:Perform trace-based impact analysis;
:Create a bounded increment and propagate forward\nthrough every affected downstream level;
:Reconcile any emergency downstream change\ninto its authoritative source;
:Obtain new G2–G7 evidence as applicable;
:Release, observe and close the change record;
stop
@enduml
